{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.HookLengthFormula","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridgeTwo","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PieceAGeneral"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF.numSYT_mul_hookProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF.numSYT_mul_hookProduct","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookProductHLF.lean#L88-L103","doc":"**Frame–Robinson–Thrall hook-length formula** in the `QOU.BraidKnot` register,\n**sorry-free**:\n\n  `#SYT(μ) · ∏_{c ∈ μ} h(c) = |μ|!`,\n\nequivalently `f^μ = |μ|! / ∏ h(c)`. Stated multiplicatively so it lives over `ℕ`\n(`hookProduct_pos` makes the division form well-posed).\n\nThis is the brick-1 target formerly carried as a cited `sorry` in\n`QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau`; it is now discharged by composing the tableau-count\nbridge, the hook bridge above, and the proved geometric HLF. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF.hookProduct_eq_hookLengthProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF.hookProduct_eq_hookLengthProduct","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookProductHLF.lean#L80-L86","doc":"**The hook bridge.** The two hook-length *products* over `μ`'s cells agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF.hookLength_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF.hookLength_eq","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookProductHLF.lean#L73-L78","doc":"**The hook bridge, cellwise.** On a genuine cell the two hook-length definitions agree:\n`BraidKnot`'s filter-counted `arm + leg + 1` is the geometric `armLength + legLength + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF.legCard_eq_legLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF.legCard_eq_legLength","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookProductHLF.lean#L58-L71","doc":"**Leg bridge.** For a genuine cell `(i, j) ∈ μ`, the `Finset.filter` count of cells\nstrictly below `(i, j)` in column `j` — `BraidKnot`'s leg — equals the geometric leg\nlength `μ.colLen j - i - 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF.armCard_eq_armLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookProductHLF.armCard_eq_armLength","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookProductHLF.lean#L43-L56","doc":"**Arm bridge.** For a genuine cell `(i, j) ∈ μ`, the `Finset.filter` count of cells\nstrictly to the right of `(i, j)` in row `i` — `BraidKnot`'s arm — equals the geometric\narm length `μ.rowLen i - j - 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}